      "math_academy_id": "e-3625",
      "problem": "Given that $f(x)=4e^x+ 3x^4 - x^2,$ find $f'(x).$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the addition and the power rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{ \n                          f'(x)             &= \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\left(4e^x+3x^{4} - x^2 \\right)\\\n                                             &= \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\left(4e^x\\right)+\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\left(3x^{4}\\right) -\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\left(x^{2}\\right) \\\n\t\t\t\t\t     &= 4\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\left(e^x\\right)+3\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\left(x^{4}\\right) - 2x \\\t\t\t\n                                             &=  4 e^x+  3 \\cdot 4x^{3} - 2x \\\n                                             &=  4 e^x+  12x^{3} - 2x.\n}\n$$",
